#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:10
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:12
msgid ""
"Syncthing supports archiving the old version of a file when it is deleted or "
"replaced with a newer version from the cluster. This is called \"file "
"versioning\" and uses one of the available *versioning strategies* described "
"below. File versioning is configured per folder and defaults to \"no file "
"versioning\", i.e. no old copies of files are kept."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:19
msgid "Trash Can File Versioning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:21
msgid ""
"This versioning strategy emulates the common \"trash can\" approach. When a "
"file is deleted or replaced due to a change on a remote device, it is a "
"moved to the trash can in the ``.stversions`` folder. If a file with the "
"same name was already in the trash can it is replaced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:26
msgid ""
"A configuration option is available to clean the trash can from files older "
"than a specified number of days. If this is set to a positive number of "
"days, files will be removed when they have been in the trash can that long. "
"Setting this to zero prevents any files from being removed from the trash "
"can automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:33
msgid "Simple File Versioning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:35
msgid ""
"With \"Simple File Versioning\" files are moved to the ``.stversions`` "
"folder (inside your shared folder) when replaced or deleted on a remote "
"device. This option also takes a value in an input titled \"Keep Versions\" "
"which tells Syncthing how many old versions of the file it should keep. For "
"example, if you set this value to 5, if a file is replaced 5 times on a "
"remote device, you will see 5 time-stamped versions on that file in the \"."
"stversions\" folder on the other devices sharing the same folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:44
msgid "Staggered File Versioning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:46
msgid ""
"With \"Staggered File Versioning\" files are also moved to a different "
"folder when replaced or deleted on a remote device (just like \"Simple File "
"Versioning\"), however, versions are automatically deleted if they are older "
"than the maximum age or exceed the number of files allowed in an interval."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:51
msgid ""
"With this versioning method it's possible to specify where the versions are "
"stored, with the default being the ``.stversions`` folder inside the normal "
"folder path. If you set a custom version path, please ensure that it's on "
"the same partition or filesystem as the regular folder path, as moving files "
"there may otherwise fail. You can use an absolute path (this is recommended) "
"or a relative path. Relative paths are interpreted relative to Syncthing's "
"current or startup directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:59
msgid ""
"The following intervals are used and they each have a maximum number of "
"files that will be kept for each."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:62
msgid "1 Hour"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:63
msgid "For the first hour, the most recent version is kept every 30 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:64
msgid "1 Day"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:65
msgid "For the first day, the most recent version is kept every hour."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:66
msgid "30 Days"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:67
msgid "For the first 30 days, the most recent version is kept every day."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:68
msgid "Until Maximum Age"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:69
msgid ""
"The maximum time to keep a version in days. For example, to keep replaced or "
"deleted files in the \".stversions\" folder for an entire year, use 365. If "
"only or 10 days, use 10. **Note: Set to 0 to keep versions forever.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:74
msgid "External File Versioning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:76
msgid ""
"This versioning method delegates the decision on what to do to an external "
"command (program or script). The only configuration option is the name of "
"the command. This should be an absolute path name. Just prior to a file "
"being replaced, the command will be run with two parameters: the path to the "
"folder, and the path to the file within the folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:83
msgid "Example for Unixes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:85
msgid ""
"Lets say I want to keep the latest version of each file as they are replaced "
"or removed; essentially I want a \"trash can\"-like behavior. For this, I "
"create the following script and store it as ``/Users/jb/bin/onlylatest.sh`` "
"(i.e. the ``bin`` directory in my home directory):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:90
msgid ""
"#!/bin/sh\n"
"set -eu\n"
"\n"
"# Where I want my versions stored\n"
"versionspath=~/.trashcan\n"
"\n"
"# The parameters we get from Syncthing\n"
"folderpath=\"$1\"\n"
"filepath=\"$2\"\n"
"\n"
"# First ensure the dir where we need to store the file exists\n"
"outpath=`dirname \"$versionspath/$filepath\"`\n"
"mkdir -p \"$outpath\"\n"
"# Then move the file there\n"
"mv -f \"$folderpath/$filepath\" \"$versionspath/$filepath\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:108
msgid ""
"I must ensure that the script has execute permissions (``chmod 755 "
"onlylatest.sh``), then configure Syncthing with the above path as the "
"command name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:112
msgid ""
"Lets assume I have a folder \"default\" in ~/Sync, and that within that "
"folder there is a file ``docs/letter.txt`` that is being replaced or "
"deleted. The script will be called as if I ran this from the command line::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:116
msgid "$ /Users/jb/bin/onlylatest.sh /Users/jb/Sync docs/letter.txt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:118
msgid ""
"The script will then move the file in question to ``~/.trashcan/docs/letter."
"txt``, replacing any previous version of that letter that may already have "
"been there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:123
msgid "Example for Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:125
msgid ""
"On Windows we can use a batch script to perform the same \"trash can\"-like "
"behavior as mentioned above. I created the following script and saved it as "
"``C:\\Users\\mfrnd\\Scripts\\onlylatest.bat``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:129
msgid ""
"@echo off\n"
"\n"
":: We need command extensions for mkdir to create intermediate folders in "
"one go\n"
"setlocal EnableExtensions\n"
"\n"
":: Where I want my versions stored\n"
"set VERSIONS_PATH=%USERPROFILE%\\.trashcan\n"
"\n"
":: The parameters we get from Syncthing, '~' removes quotes if any\n"
"set FOLDER_PATH=%~1\n"
"set FILE_PATH=%~2\n"
"\n"
":: First ensure the dir where we need to store the file exists\n"
"for %%F in (\"%VERSIONS_PATH%\\%FILE_PATH%\") do set OUTPUT_PATH=%%~dpF\n"
"if not exist \"%OUTPUT_PATH%\" mkdir \"%OUTPUT_PATH%\" || exit /B\n"
"\n"
":: Finally move the file, overwrite existing file if any\n"
"move /Y \"%FOLDER_PATH%\\%FILE_PATH%\" \"%VERSIONS_PATH%\\%FILE_PATH%\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:150
msgid ""
"Finally, I set ``C:\\Users\\mfrnd\\Scripts\\onlylatest.bat`` as command name "
"in Syncthing."
msgstr ""
